= Stakeholder - Resident with dementia [ST-01] =

//Who is affected. In the Foundation, captured by exactly two things: the values they hold, and their relationship to other Stakeholders. A full behavioral Persona is built later, in the Specification, for Direct Stakeholders only.//

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-01
|Name|Resident with dementia
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. The stakeholder set is derived from SA-01 to SA-03. Values and priorities are the group's reasoning.
|Type|Direct - interacts with the System during the activity
|Values and motivations|(((
- HV-02: Dignity (high)

- HV-01: Autonomy (high)

- HV-05: Well-being (high)

- HV-04: Competence (medium)

- HV-03: Privacy (medium)
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Receives day-to-day support from ST-02 care workers. ST-03 family members may visit and be involved in care decisions, including consent. Receives medical care from ST-05, and lives in a home run by ST-04.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-01, SA-02; holds → HV-01, HV-02, HV-03, HV-04, HV-05; appears-in → PS-01, PS-02; elaborated-as → HP-01 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Care home staff member [ST-02] =

//Who is affected. In the Foundation, captured by exactly two things: the values they hold, and their relationship to other Stakeholders. A full behavioral Persona is built later, in the Specification, for Direct Stakeholders only.//

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-02
|Name|Care home staff member
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. The stakeholder set is derived from SA-01 to SA-03. Values and priorities are the group's reasoning.
|Type|Direct - receives handover requests and reviews the session record
|Values and motivations|(((
- HV-05: Well-being (high)

- HV-06: Attentive care (high)

- HV-02: Dignity (medium)

- HV-01: Autonomy (medium) - endorses it for residents, but weighs it against the time available

- HV-04: Competence (medium)

- HV-03: Privacy (medium) - for residents, and against surveillance of their own work
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Supports several ST-01 residents per shift. Employed by ST-04. Keeps ST-03 informed about their relative, and coordinates with ST-05 on medication and health.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-03; supports → SA-01, SA-02; holds → HV-01 to HV-06; appears-in → PS-01, PS-02; elaborated-as → HP-02 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Family members of Resident [ST-03] =

//Who is affected. In the Foundation, captured by exactly two things: the values they hold, and their relationship to other Stakeholders. A full behavioral Persona is built later, in the Specification, for Direct Stakeholders only.//

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-03
|Name|Family members of Resident
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. The stakeholder set is derived from SA-01 to SA-03. Values and priorities are the group's reasoning.
|Type|Indirect - affected by outcomes, does not interact with the System and does not receive its records
|Values and motivations|(((
- HV-05: Well-being (high)

- HV-02: Dignity (high)

- HV-01: Autonomy (medium)

- HV-06: Attentive care (medium)

- HV-03: Privacy (low) - may want more information about their relative than the resident would choose to share
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Relatives of ST-01. In contact with ST-02 about their relative's care, and may be involved in consent decisions on ST-01's behalf.

== Graph edges ==

holds → HV-01, HV-02, HV-03, HV-05, HV-06.

= Stakeholder - Management or the Owners of the care home [ST-04] =

//Who is affected. In the Foundation, captured by exactly two things: the values they hold, and their relationship to other Stakeholders. A full behavioral Persona is built later, in the Specification, for Direct Stakeholders only.//

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-04
|Name|Management or the Owners of the care home
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. The stakeholder set is derived from SA-01 to SA-03. Values and priorities are the group's reasoning.
|Type|Indirect - decides on adopting the System, does not interact with it
|Values and motivations|(((
- HV-06: Attentive care (high) - staffing and workload

- HV-05: Well-being (high) - quality of care

- HV-03: Privacy (medium) - data-protection obligations for residents and staff

- HV-02: Dignity (medium)
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Employs ST-02. Responsible for the home's quality of care, staffing and data protection, and for the living environment of ST-01.

== Graph edges ==

holds → HV-02, HV-03, HV-05, HV-06.

= Stakeholder - Medical staff: GP, Nurse [ST-05] =

//Who is affected. In the Foundation, captured by exactly two things: the values they hold, and their relationship to other Stakeholders. A full behavioral Persona is built later, in the Specification, for Direct Stakeholders only.//

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-05
|Name|Medical staff: GP, Nurse
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. The stakeholder set is derived from SA-01 to SA-03. Values and priorities are the group's reasoning.
|Type|Indirect - responsible for care plans and medication, does not interact with the System
|Values and motivations|(((
- HV-05: Well-being (high)

- HV-03: Privacy (medium) - medical confidentiality

- HV-01: Autonomy (medium)
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Prescribes and reviews ST-01's medication and health. Relies on ST-02 to carry out care plans day to day.

== Graph edges ==

holds → HV-01, HV-03, HV-05.